The purpose of this article is to:
(1) Provide environmentally sound, cost-efficient refuse disposal in accordance with the Solid Waste Management Act, O.C.G.A. § 12-8-20 et seq.;
(2) Enhance operation of the facilities of the county environmental management department;
(3) Maximize the useful life of the solid waste disposal facilities;
(4) Protect human health and the environment;
(5) Provide for and regulate the collection and disposal of solid waste in the county;
(6) Prohibit, throughout the unincorporated area of the county, littering on public or private property; and
(7) Curb thereby the desecration of the beauty of the county which is harmful to the health, welfare, and safety of its citizens, and prohibit the disposal of out-of-county waste in the county solid waste management facilities.
(Ord. No. 023-24, 12-17-24)

